# Campaign stage 0: today's engine, unchanged, with 100, then 500, then 1,000
# jobs running at once, in one cell of three engines.
#
# Each job lasts two minutes. A step delivers pushes at the rate that keeps
# its number of jobs running, lets them pile up for two minutes, and is
# measured for the three minutes after. The first three steps' jobs write
# nothing but their first and last lines; the last three write ten lines of
# log a second each, so that what logs cost can be told from what jobs cost.
#
# NAME JOBS SECS HOLD [LPS] [KIB]
quiet-100    100 120 180
quiet-500    500 120 180
quiet-1000  1000 120 180
logs-100     100 120 180 10
logs-500     500 120 180 10
logs-1000   1000 120 180 10
